1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
Can we fit nearly
12,000 years of Turkey

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,459
into one minute?
Let's find out.

3
00:00:05,499 --> 00:00:08,339
Around 9500 BC,
hunters build

4
00:00:08,379 --> 00:00:11,703
giant stone pillars
at Göbekli Tepe.

5
00:00:11,743 --> 00:00:14,363
Around 1600 BC, the Hittites

6
00:00:14,403 --> 00:00:16,943
make Hattusa their
walled capital.

7
00:00:16,983 --> 00:00:20,043
In the year 330, Constantine
makes Constantinople

8
00:00:20,083 --> 00:00:22,833
the new capital of Rome.

9
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:25,393
In 537, Hagia Sophia opens,

10
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:29,558
with a dome that seems
to hang in the air.

11
00:00:29,598 --> 00:00:32,658
In 1453, Ottoman
cannons break the walls,

12
00:00:32,698 --> 00:00:35,439
and Constantinople falls.

13
00:00:35,479 --> 00:00:38,019
In the 1500s,
Suleiman the Magnificent

14
00:00:38,059 --> 00:00:42,770
rules a vast empire
on three continents.

15
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:46,250
In 1923, Atatürk founds
the Republic of Turkey,

16
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:49,262
with Ankara as its capital.

17
00:00:49,302 --> 00:00:52,442
Today, about 86 million
people call Turkey home,

18
00:00:52,482 --> 00:00:54,533
on two continents.

19
00:00:54,573 --> 00:00:58,350
Have you tried Turkish
tea? Tell us below.

